er a new tag  obviously this means that zack is not  banned in louisiana and continues to  play there if he likes  but it goes to show how someone who has  been banned or accused of sexual  misconduct  can continue to be a part of the  community and potentially harm more  people  even after they've been banned again i  am not saying that zack 100  will abuse someone and i am not saying  that he 100 abused someone  all i am saying is that he is an example  of a player who is clearly banned  who is still able to participate in the  community and that fact  concerns me what happens when smash  tournaments return on  mass and each tournament organizer in  every state has their own unique  ban list i understand this match is  grassroots that there's no global body  deciding who is and isn't allowed in the  convention centers of north america  but i don't think that makes the end  result palatable do you institute age  minimums for tournaments do you make  people come with a chaperone  do you get rid of after parties even  though that would mean that people just  have their after-parties in their own  hotel rooms i don't have the answer  right now  look i love smash i think that it's a  community full of wonderful people who  do not deserve to play in the same space  as creeps and  people defending those creeps i don't  know what tournament organizers are  doing behind the scenes to protect the  community from predators  i just only hope that they're doing  [Music]  something  [Music]  you

